 "action_summary": "The owner split the problem into exact recall, which is solved and shipped, and generalization, which is not, and asked that the second be solved in the fastest correct way. The tree already holds the first-principles answer in canonical/runtime/applicability_v1, which is wired into macro_v1, precondition_discovery_v1 and contrast_selection_v1 and states that the missing quantity is not more demonstrations but the STATE each outcome happened in, and that a caller may only withhold a plan on IDENTIFIED. The skill store never asks it anything. This round measures what actually decides where a shipped skill applies, by perturbing or deleting one declared field at a time and re-running the rule over a probe corpus of eight sources declared before any measurement: six of the eight fields, including language, error_class and domain, are DECORATIVE on all five skills, and only pattern_tokens and replacement_tokens constrain behaviour. The positive control is what makes that mean something -- perturbing the matcher does change behaviour, in the same run, on the same corpus. Every shipped skill carries verified_hits 1 and zero states, so applicability_v1 returns UNDETERMINED for five of five and none may be called generalizing under the tree's own law. A count is not a state; growing it to a thousand would add no scope. The expected stronger result was NOT found and is recorded as a negative: no rule rewrote another language's bytes, each refused seven of eight probes, and those refusals come from the token matcher rather than from the declared class, because a refusal from syntax can say only that the text did not match and never that the match is outside the class. Narrowness is not a scope. Nothing here claims a capability: the deliverable is an instrument, a ledger, a label that can be earned, and the price of the observation that would earn it.",
